#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:9
msgid "Learning about services - tutorial"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:11
msgid ""
"Services are one of the communication types used to exchange data in a ROS "
"system. This article walks you through using command-line tools to examine "
"and call services between nodes. A hands-on exercise with Turtlesim helps "
"you understand how the call-and-response model works in the ROS graph."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:15
msgid "**Area: Framework | Content-type: tutorial | Experience: beginner**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:19
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:22
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:24
msgid ""
"Services use a call-and-response model: a client sends a request to a "
"server, which processes it and returns a response. Unlike topics, services "
"only provide data when specifically called, so they are not suited for "
"continuous data streams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:27
msgid ""
"For more information, see :doc:`About services <../../../About-Services>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:30
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:32
msgid ""
"Make sure you understand the concepts of :doc:`nodes <../../../../nodes/"
"Working-with-nodes/Understanding-ROS2-Nodes/Understanding-ROS2-Nodes>` and :"
"doc:`topics <../../../topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-"
"Topics>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:33
msgid ""
"Make sure you have installed the :doc:`turtlesim package <../../../../../Get-"
"Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:36
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:39
msgid ""
"Do not forget to source ROS in every new terminal you open. See :doc:"
