#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:43
msgid "1 Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:45
msgid ""
"You need a running system with services to inspect. Start the ``/turtlesim`` "
"node, which provides the application services you will examine and call "
"later (such as ``/clear`` and ``/spawn``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:48
msgid "Open a new terminal and run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:50
msgid "$ ros2 run turtlesim turtlesim_node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:54
msgid "Open another terminal and run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:56
msgid "$ ros2 run turtlesim turtle_teleop_key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:60
msgid ""
"Running this node along with ``turtlesim_node`` lets you see that each node "
"exposes its own set of parameter services when you list services."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:62
msgid ""
"Leave both terminals running while you work through the Turtlesim examples "
"below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:65
msgid "2 List the active services"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:67
msgid ""
"Listing services is useful when you need to discover what you can call on a "
"running system. To list all the services currently active in the system, in "
"a new terminal, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:70
msgid "$ ros2 service list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:74
msgid "The terminal returns the active service names:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:76
msgid ""
"/clear\n"
"/kill\n"
"/reset\n"
"/spawn\n"
"/teleop_turtle/describe_parameters\n"
"/teleop_turtle/get_parameter_types\n"
"/teleop_turtle/get_parameters\n"
"/teleop_turtle/list_parameters\n"
"/teleop_turtle/set_parameters\n"
"/teleop_turtle/set_parameters_atomically\n"
"/turtle1/set_pen\n"
"/turtle1/teleport_absolute\n"
"/turtle1/teleport_relative\n"
"/turtlesim/describe_parameters\n"
"/turtlesim/get_parameter_types\n"
"/turtlesim/get_parameters\n"
"/turtlesim/list_parameters\n"
"/turtlesim/set_parameters\n"
"/turtlesim/set_parameters_atomically"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:98
msgid ""
"Both Turtlesim nodes have the same six services with ``parameters`` in their "
"names. Nearly every node in ROS has these infrastructure services on which "
"parameters are based. Parameters are covered in :doc:`Learning about "
"parameters <../../../../parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-"
"ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters>`. In this tutorial, the "
"parameter services will not be discussed in detail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:103
msgid ""
"The turtlesim-specific services are ``/clear``, ``/kill``, ``/reset``, ``/"
"spawn``, ``/turtle1/set_pen``, ``/turtle1/teleport_absolute``, and ``/"
"turtle1/teleport_relative``. Some of these services were covered in the :doc:"
"`Using turtlesim, ros2, and rqt <../../../../../Get-Started/Introducing-"
"Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim>` tutorial."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:108
msgid "3 View the service type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:110
msgid ""
"Before you call a service, you need its type so you know what request and "
"response data it expects. Services have types that describe how that data is "
"structured. Service types are defined similarly to topic types, except "
"service types have two parts: one message for the request and another for "
"the response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:114
msgid "To find out the type of a service, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:116
msgid "$ ros2 service type <service_name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:120
msgid ""
"For example, to check Turtlesim's ``/clear`` service, open a new terminal "
"and run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:122
msgid "$ ros2 service type /clear"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:126
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:174
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:277
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:301
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:319
msgid "The terminal returns:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:128
msgid "std_srvs/srv/Empty"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:132
msgid ""
"The ``Empty`` type means the service call sends no data when making a "
"request and receives no data when receiving a response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:135
msgid "3.1 View a list of all active services"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:137
msgid ""
"When you need a quick overview of every service and its type together, "
"append the ``--show-types`` option (abbreviated as ``-t``) to the ``list`` "
"command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:139
msgid "$ ros2 service list -t"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:143
msgid "The terminal returns each service with its type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:145
msgid ""
"/clear [std_srvs/srv/Empty]\n"
"/kill [turtlesim_msgs/srv/Kill]\n"
"/reset [std_srvs/srv/Empty]\n"
"/spawn [turtlesim_msgs/srv/Spawn]\n"
"...\n"
"/turtle1/set_pen [turtlesim_msgs/srv/SetPen]\n"
"/turtle1/teleport_absolute [turtlesim_msgs/srv/TeleportAbsolute]\n"
"/turtle1/teleport_relative [turtlesim_msgs/srv/TeleportRelative]\n"
"..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:158
msgid "4 View the information about a particular service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:160
msgid ""
"Use ``ros2 service info`` to see a service's type and how many clients and "
"servers are using it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:162
msgid "To inspect a particular service, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:164
msgid "$ ros2 service info <service_name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:168
msgid "For example, to check the ``/clear`` service, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:170
msgid "$ ros2 service info /clear"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:176
msgid ""
"Type: std_srvs/srv/Empty\n"
"Clients count: 0\n"
"Services count: 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:182
msgid ""
"To see more detail about the same service, including which node provides it, "
"append the ``--verbose`` (or ``-v``) option:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:184
msgid "$ ros2 service info --verbose <service_name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:189
msgid ""
"The ``--verbose`` option is available on Lyrical. Older distributions do not "
