msgid "$ ros2 service info --verbose /clear"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:198
msgid ""
"Besides the basic type and client/server counts, the verbose result also "
"shows which node provides the service and the low-level connection details "
"from the ROS middleware (RMW). You mainly need those details when "
"troubleshooting connection problems with a service. The ``Endpoint count`` "
"value is ``2`` for DDS-based RMW implementations (``rmw_connextdds``, "
"``rmw_cyclonedds``, ``rmw_fastrtps``) because DDS creates two endpoints per "
"service server: one for request and one for response."
msgstr ""

