#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:279
msgid ""
"/clear\n"
"/reset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:285
msgid "6 View the arguments of the call and response for a service type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:287
msgid ""
"Before you call a service with arguments, inspect its type so you know which "
"fields the request needs and what the response contains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:289
msgid "To inspect a service type's structure, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:291
msgid "$ ros2 interface show <type_name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:295
msgid "Try the following command on the ``/clear`` service's type, ``Empty``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:297
msgid "$ ros2 interface show std_srvs/srv/Empty"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:303
msgid "---"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:307
msgid ""
"The ``---`` separates the request structure from the response structure. The "
"``Empty`` type doesn't send or receive any data, so its structure is blank "
"above and below the separator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:310
msgid ""
"Let's introspect a service with a type that sends and receives data, like ``/"
"spawn``. From the results of ``ros2 service list -t``, we know ``/spawn``'s "
"type is ``turtlesim_msgs/srv/Spawn``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:313
msgid ""
"To see the request and response arguments of the ``/spawn`` service, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:315
msgid "$ ros2 interface show turtlesim_msgs/srv/Spawn"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:321
msgid ""
"float32 x\n"
"float32 y\n"
"float32 theta\n"
"string name # Optional.  A unique name will be created and returned if this "
"is empty\n"
"---\n"
"string name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:330
msgid ""
"The text above the separator lists the arguments needed to call ``/spawn``: "
"``x``, ``y`` and ``theta`` determine the 2D pose of the spawned turtle, and "
"``name`` is optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:333
msgid ""
"The text below the separator line is the response. In this case, the "
"response is the name assigned to the new turtle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:337
msgid "7 Call a service from the command line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:339
msgid ""
"Now that you know the service names, types, and argument layouts, you can "
"send requests from the command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:341
msgid "To call a service, use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:343
msgid "$ ros2 service call <service_name> <service_type> <arguments>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:347
msgid ""
"The ``<arguments>`` part is optional. For example, ``Empty`` typed services "
"don't have any arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:350
msgid "$ ros2 service call /clear std_srvs/srv/Empty"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:354
msgid "This clears the Turtlesim window of any lines drawn by the turtle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:358
msgid ""
"Next, spawn a new turtle by calling ``/spawn`` with arguments. Arguments in "
"a service call from the command line must be in YAML syntax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:361
