#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:483
msgid "What is the difference between a service and a topic?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:484
msgid ""
"Topics use a publish-subscribe model where data is broadcast continuously to "
"any subscriber. Services use a call-and-response model: a client sends a "
"specific request and waits for a single response. Use topics for continuous "
"data streams and services for discrete, one-time interactions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:488
msgid "Why do I see so many services with ``parameters`` in their names?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:489
msgid ""
"Nearly every ROS node automatically exposes a set of parameter services. "
"These are infrastructure services that the parameter system is built on. "
"This tutorial focuses on application-specific services; parameter services "
"are covered in the parameters tutorial."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:493
msgid ""
"What does the ``---`` separator mean in ``ros2 interface show`` for a "
"service?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:494
msgid ""
"The ``---`` separates the request fields from the response fields. For "
"``Empty`` typed services, both halves are blank because no data is sent or "
"received."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:497
msgid "When should I use a service instead of a topic?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:498
msgid ""
"Use a service when you need a discrete, one-time interaction with a "
"guaranteed response, such as spawning an entity or resetting a node's state. "
"For continuous data streams, use a topic. For long-running goals that "
"provide feedback, consider using an action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:502
msgid "Why does ``ros2 service echo`` show no output?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-Services.rst:503
msgid ""
"Service introspection is disabled by default. Enable it on both the client "
"and the server. In this tutorial, do that by running the ``ros2 param set`` "
"commands on the demo nodes before you start ``ros2 service echo``. Keep the "
"demo launch running in its own terminal so the client keeps sending requests."
msgstr ""
